Stopped thinking
Yes, I understand the issue now. 👍

I looked carefully at your screenshots, and this is not a React problem. It's a CSS layout problem.

I can see three issues:
❌ Issue 1: The signup card is extremely tall
Because of that:

The logo and heading are getting pushed out of the screen.

Only the middle of the form is visible.

❌ Issue 2: Huge white space on both sides
This usually happens because you have something like:

.signup-card{
    width:40%;
}
or

margin-left:200px;
margin-right:200px;
Instead, we should let Flexbox center the card.

❌ Issue 3: Black bars at the bottom
Those black sections are not from the signup page.

They usually happen because:

body

#root

.signup-page

don't have the correct height.

Let's fix it properly (Professional way)
Step 1
Show me your entire Signup.css.

Don't send only part of it.

Copy and paste the complete file.

Step 2
Also show me your index.css (or App.css if you're using that).

Especially I want to see if you have something like:

body{
...
}

#root{
...
}
I already suspect one mistake
Earlier, when we were learning, I asked you to experiment with heights.

You may still have something like:

.signup-page{
    height:200vh;
}
or

padding-top:100px;
padding-bottom:100px;
or

margin-top:150px;
That would produce exactly the kind of layout shown in your screenshots.

Don't worry
We'll fix this together. I don't want to just give you CSS—I want you to understand why it broke.

Once you paste:

✅ Signup.css

✅ index.css (or App.css if that's where your global styles are)

I'll go through them line by line, point out the mistakes, explain each one, and help you make the page look like a professional signup screen.


